  "notes": "Means having all necessary equipment or features in place. Frequently seen in real estate listings, hotel descriptions, and facility advertisements.\n\nFORMS:\n{完|かん} (complete) + {備|び} (equipped, prepared).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- エアコン{完備|かんび}: air conditioning included\n- {冷暖房|れいだんぼう}{完備|かんび}: heating and cooling equipped\n- {設備|せつび}{完備|かんび}: fully equipped facilities\n- {駐車場|ちゅうしゃじょう}{完備|かんび}: parking available\n\nUSAGE:\nAs a する verb: {設備|せつび}を{完備|かんび}する (to fully equip with facilities). As a standalone descriptor in listings: エアコン{完備|かんび} (A/C equipped — no verb needed).",
